# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
build/
dist/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.claude/

# Environment
.env

# Data — large, gated, and reproducible from the evaluation subset IDs.
# data/evaluation_subset.json is NOT ignored: it defines reproducibility.
# These directories are created at runtime by paths.ensure_dir().
data/raw/
data/processed/

# Transcript dumps from `show_run.py` and friends. MALT is gated: METR controls
# who receives the transcripts, so verbatim run text must never be committed,
# whatever it happens to be named locally.
prompted.txt
*_transcript.txt
*_transcripts.txt
transcripts/

# Working notes kept locally, deliberately not published: the original research
# plan and the adversarial review brief written for a reviewer.
notes.md
docs/handoff.md
docs/experiments.md

# Experiment outputs. The figures for the current run are tracked so the repo
# carries the result without a reader needing dataset access and an API key; the
# CSVs and results.jsonl are not, because they quote monitor reasoning derived
# from gated MALT transcripts. Re-run scripts/figures.py to regenerate.
# Un-ignoring a path requires un-ignoring each parent directory first — git
# never descends into an excluded directory to find negations inside it.
results/*
!results/sandbagging-fixed/
results/sandbagging-fixed/*
!results/sandbagging-fixed/figures/

# LLM response cache
.cache/

# OS
.DS_Store
